From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:52:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FAKE: keep adbd running on Cuttlefish whatever the USB config

Cuttlefish's adbd uses vsock, not a USB gadget. AERA sets
sys.usb.config=none at start, and the recovery init.rc then stops adbd,
which leaves the lab VM with no adb. On real devices this is the right
behaviour, so this stays a devicelab-only fake, gated on
ro.hardware=cutf_cvm.
---
 etc/init.rc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/etc/init.rc b/etc/init.rc
index c7f3d04..e16d898 100644
--- a/etc/init.rc
+++ b/etc/init.rc
@@ -257,3 +257,9 @@ on property:sys.usb.config=fastboot && property:sys.usb.ffs.ready=1 && property:
     symlink /config/usb_gadget/g1/functions/ffs.fastboot /config/usb_gadget/g1/configs/b.1/f1
     write /config/usb_gadget/g1/UDC ${sys.usb.controller}
     setprop sys.usb.state ${sys.usb.config}
+
+# FAKE (devicelab patches-cf, Cuttlefish only): Cuttlefish's adbd talks over
+# vsock, not a USB gadget, so stopping it when AERA sets the USB config to
+# "none" only cuts the lab off. Defined last so it runs after the stops above.
+on property:sys.usb.config=* && property:ro.hardware=cutf_cvm
+    start adbd
-- 
